item.description:
POST /products scenarios S1-S12 (internal/routes/product_routes.go). Run in order.

Status rule: "1" = active (A), anything else = inactive (I).
moq is optional: missing or empty => 1 (written to store_products when BOS/FOS is added).
S4 and S10 show "inserted" only when TEST-SKU-0001/0002 do not exist yet. Run this cleanup SQL after testing (and before re-running):

BEGIN;
DELETE FROM picklist_product_assignations WHERE picklist_product_id IN (SELECT id FROM picklist_products WHERE product_id IN (SELECT id FROM products WHERE sku IN ('TEST-SKU-0001','TEST-SKU-0002')));
DELETE FROM picklist_products WHERE product_id IN (SELECT id FROM products WHERE sku IN ('TEST-SKU-0001','TEST-SKU-0002'));
DELETE FROM product_location  WHERE product_id IN (SELECT id FROM products WHERE sku IN ('TEST-SKU-0001','TEST-SKU-0002'));
DELETE FROM store_location    WHERE name IN (SELECT 'Virtual FoS - ' || id FROM products WHERE sku IN ('TEST-SKU-0001','TEST-SKU-0002'));
DELETE FROM store_products    WHERE product_id IN (SELECT id FROM products WHERE sku IN ('TEST-SKU-0001','TEST-SKU-0002'));
DELETE FROM products          WHERE sku IN ('TEST-SKU-0001','TEST-SKU-0002');
DELETE FROM product_brands    WHERE external_id = 'TESTBRANDAPI';
COMMIT;

POST /boh scenarios B1-B12 (internal/routes/boh_routes.go). Run in order.

storeId is stores.external_id (not stores.id). POS mode is disabled, so appMode is always "default".
B1, B6 and B8 show "inserted" only before cleanup. This cleanup restores the values from before the tests:

BEGIN;
DELETE FROM boh WHERE date = '2026-10-14' AND (store_id, product_id) IN ((112, 129185), (333502389, 785490), (101, 132510));
UPDATE store_products SET total_qty = 11 WHERE store_id = 112       AND product_id = 129185;
UPDATE store_products SET total_qty = 0  WHERE store_id = 333502389 AND product_id = 785490;
DELETE FROM store_products WHERE store_id = 101 AND product_id = 132510;
COMMIT;

POST /deliveries scenarios D1-D15b (internal/routes/delivery_routes.go). Run in order.

storeId is stores.external_id. Post-feed processing (put stock away, finish the delivery) is DISABLED, so postProcessing is always "disabled" and deliveries stay planned.
D9/D10/D12/D13 write activity_logs rows. D1, D11 and D15 show "inserted" only before cleanup. Cleanup:

BEGIN;
DELETE FROM delivery_product_assignations WHERE delivery_product_id IN (
  SELECT dp.id FROM delivery_products dp JOIN delivery_units du ON du.id = dp.delivery_unit_id
  JOIN deliveries d ON d.id = du.delivery_id WHERE d.asn IN (990000001, 990000002, 990000003));
DELETE FROM delivery_products WHERE delivery_unit_id IN (
  SELECT du.id FROM delivery_units du JOIN deliveries d ON d.id = du.delivery_id WHERE d.asn IN (990000001, 990000002, 990000003));
DELETE FROM delivery_units WHERE delivery_id IN (SELECT id FROM deliveries WHERE asn IN (990000001, 990000002, 990000003));
DELETE FROM deliveries WHERE asn IN (990000001, 990000002, 990000003);
DELETE FROM activity_logs WHERE event = 'DELIVERY_STORE_NOT_FOUND_SKIPPED' AND metadata->'stores' @> '[7777]';
DELETE FROM activity_logs WHERE event = 'DELIVERY_PRODUCTS_NOT_FOUND_SKIPPED' AND metadata->'products' @> '[{"asn": 990000001}]';
DELETE FROM activity_logs WHERE event = 'DELIVERY_FEED_RECORDS_SKIPPED' AND store_id = 1221 AND created_at >= '2026-10-14';
COMMIT;

POST /stocktake scenarios T1-T12 (internal/routes/stocktake_routes.go). Run in order.

storeId is stores.external_id. Counts REPLACE location quantities (split evenly over the locations); store_products is not updated.
T7 is skipped while the open-picklist check is disabled. T12 needs a temporary SQL toggle (see its description). T1 and T6 show "inserted" only before cleanup. Cleanup restores the values from before the tests:

BEGIN;
UPDATE product_location SET "case" = NULL, units = NULL, qty = 0
WHERE id IN (15726087, 21496139, 21496172, 21496626, 39631764, 39631765);
DELETE FROM stock_takes WHERE (store_id, product_id) IN ((102, 129465), (333502389, 785490));
COMMIT;

POST /pos scenarios P1-P14 (internal/routes/pos_routes.go). Run in order: each step depends on the counters left by the previous one.

storeId is stores.external_id. Default app mode: new picklists get the type "department" ("moq" is a commented line for POS mode).
Every test uses register 77. The tests only pass on the starting values; run this cleanup after testing (and before re-running):

BEGIN;
DELETE FROM pos WHERE register = 77;
DELETE FROM picklist_products WHERE picklist_id = 51570 AND product_id = 129468;
CREATE TEMP TABLE test_pl AS SELECT id FROM picklists WHERE store_id = 101 AND department_id = 66 AND status = 'N' AND name = 'BABY DIAPERS';
DELETE FROM picklist_products WHERE picklist_id IN (SELECT id FROM test_pl);
DELETE FROM picklist_groups  WHERE picklist_type_id IN (SELECT id FROM picklist_types WHERE picklist_id IN (SELECT id FROM test_pl));
DELETE FROM picklist_types   WHERE picklist_id IN (SELECT id FROM test_pl);
DELETE FROM store_picklists  WHERE picklist_id IN (SELECT id FROM test_pl);
DELETE FROM picklists        WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM test_pl);
DROP TABLE test_pl;
UPDATE picklist_products SET pickedup_quantity = 24, pickedup_cases = 2, desired_quantity = 24 WHERE id = 599165;
UPDATE store_products SET total_qty = 24, deduction_counter = 0  WHERE store_id = 101  AND product_id = 129185;
UPDATE store_products SET total_qty = 38, deduction_counter = 3  WHERE store_id = 102  AND product_id = 129468;
UPDATE store_products SET total_qty = 46, deduction_counter = 0  WHERE store_id = 101  AND product_id = 132374;
UPDATE store_products SET total_qty = 42, deduction_counter = 2  WHERE store_id = 101  AND product_id = 132375;
UPDATE store_products SET total_qty = 0,  deduction_counter = 2  WHERE store_id = 101  AND product_id = 15695037;
UPDATE store_products SET total_qty = 12, deduction_counter = 11 WHERE store_id = 1221 AND product_id = 23827981;
COMMIT;

